# 2. Step-by-Step Flow Breakdown

### Step 1: Login to Clickssy (`loginToClicktoools`)
* **Source File**: [`veolyn/netlify/functions/lib/uncodee.js`](file:///c:/Users/ankita/Downloads/flowapis/veolyn/netlify/functions/lib/uncodee.js#L5-L22)
* **Endpoint**: `POST https://clickssy.online/api/auth/login`
* **Request Body**:
  ```json
  {
    "email": "your_clickssy_email@domain.com",
    "password": "your_clickssy_password"
  }
  ```
* **Response**: Returns user metadata including the Clickssy `userId` (`data.user.id`).
* **Session Token**: Clickssy expects a session token in the format `${userId}:${email}`.

---

### Step 2: Fetch Cookies from Clickssy (`fetchCookiesFromClicktoools`)
* **Source File**: [`veolyn/netlify/functions/lib/uncodee.js`](file:///c:/Users/ankita/Downloads/flowapis/veolyn/netlify/functions/lib/uncodee.js#L24-L58)
* **Endpoint**: `POST https://clickssy.online/api/extension/verify`
* **Request Body**:
  ```json
  {
    "userId": "<userId>",
    "sessionToken": "<userId>:<email>"
  }
  ```
* **Filtering Logic**: Clickssy returns an array of raw cookies (`data.cookies`). Veolyn filters out irrelevant cookies and retains session cookies for target domains (`labs.google`, `google.com`, `next-auth`, `SID`, `HSID`, `SSID`, `APISID`, `SAPISID`, etc.):
  ```javascript
  return (data.cookies || []).filter((c) => {
    const name = c.name || c.cookie_name || "";
    const rawDom = (c.domain || c.cookie_domain || "").toLowerCase().trim();
    const cleanDom = rawDom.replace(/^\./, "");

    if (!cleanDom || cleanDom === "labs.google" || cleanDom.endsWith("labs.google") || cleanDom === "google.com" || cleanDom.endsWith("google.com")) {
      return true;
    }
    if (name.includes("next-auth") || name.includes("csrf") || ["SID", "HSID", "SSID", "APISID", "SAPISID", "NID", "OSID", "LSID", "SIDCC"].some((k) => name.includes(k))) {
      return true;
    }
    return false;
  });
  ```

