### Step 5: How Synced Cookies Are Used
* **In Proxy Requests** ([`flow-proxy.js`](file:///c:/Users/ankita/Downloads/flowapis/veolyn/netlify/functions/flow-proxy.js#L43-L46)):
  Constructs a standard HTTP cookie string:
  ```javascript
  const poolCookies = await getPoolCookies(); // fetches active cookies from DB
  const cookieHeader = poolCookies.map(c => `${c.cookie_name}=${c.cookie_value}`).join('; ');
  
  // Sent with outgoing API request to target service:
  await fetch("https://labs.google/...", {
    headers: { Cookie: cookieHeader, ... }
  });
